# AI Customer Support Request Automation

A hands-on Make.com project I built to practice using AI to classify customer support requests and route them safely.

## What I Built

The workflow receives a support request through a webhook and uses OpenAI to recommend a priority, category, action, summary, and reason.

Make.com validates the returned values before deciding whether the request can continue or needs human review.

## Workflow

**Webhook → OpenAI → Parse JSON → Validation → Router → API / Human Review → Logging**

### Key Logic

- AI output is checked against predefined values.
- Sensitive requests such as admin, credential, payroll, or server access are routed for human review.
- Invalid output is also sent for review.
- Valid normal requests can continue to the API step.
- Each request receives a unique Request ID.
- The request and result are logged in Google Sheets.

## Tools Used

- Make.com
- OpenAI
- Webhooks
- JSON / Parse JSON
- Routers & Filters
- HTTP/API
- Google Sheets
- Gmail

## What I Practiced

This project helped me practice AI classification, validation, business rules, human-in-the-loop workflows, API requests, and logging.

## Note

This is a hands-on portfolio/training project. The API endpoint is a testing endpoint used to demonstrate the HTTP/API step rather than a real customer-support backend.
